# Code Connect

Educational pnpm monorepo: React 19 SPA + NestJS 11 REST API.

## Stack
- Monorepo: pnpm workspaces (`apps/*`)
- Frontend: React 19, Vite 8, **Tailwind**, **Atomic Design**, Vitest + RTL
- Backend: NestJS 11, **REST** (resource URLs, correct verbs/status)
- Package manager: pnpm
- Git: **Conventional Commits** (`type(scope): description`)

## Structure
```
apps/web/src/components/{atoms|molecules|organisms|templates}/ + pages/
apps/api/src/   # REST controllers + services + DTOs
```

## Commands (root)
- Install: `pnpm install`
- Dev: `pnpm dev` | `pnpm dev:web` | `pnpm dev:api`
- Build: `pnpm build` | Lint: `pnpm lint`
- Test: `pnpm test:api` | `pnpm test:web` (web when configured)

## Conventions
- **Web**: one folder per component; Tailwind only; every component has `.test.tsx` (essential usage)
- **API**: plural resources, proper HTTP codes, DTOs + ValidationPipe; logic in services
- **Commits**: `feat(web):`, `fix(api):`, `test(web):`, etc. — see `.cursor/rules/git-commits.mdc`

## Agent guidelines
- Minimal diffs; match layer (atomic / REST / commit format)
- Run `pnpm lint` + relevant tests after changes
- See docs/CONVENTIONS.md, docs/ARCHITECTURE.md, AGENTS.md
